starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/gzip","state":"uploaded","size":90964,"digest":"sha256:14accda8a7d4ef47cb25b4903829fb10f011048c261a5937724a43d073c4f34d","download_count":10,"created_at":"2026-10-20T15:12:36Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T15:12:37Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/sigstore/sigstore-python/releases/download/v4.5.1/sigstore-4.5.1.tar.gz"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sigstore/sigstore-python/tarball/v4.5.1","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sigstore/sigstore-python/zipball/v4.5.1","body":"### Changed\r\n\r\n* Removed the `pyasn1` dependency and raised the minimum `cryptography` version\r\n  from 42 to 47.\r\n  ([#1866](https://github.com/sigstore/sigstore-python/pull/1866))\r\n* Certificate chain verification now uses `cryptography`, removing the\r\n  `pyOpenSSL` dependency.\r\n  ([#1867](https://github.com/sigstore/sigstore-python/pull/1867))\r\n* Switched the build backend from `flit_core` to `uv_build`.\r\n  ([#1892](https://github.com/sigstore/sigstore-python/pull/1892))\r\n\r\n### Fixed\r\n\r\n* Parsing a malformed in-toto statement now includes the underlying validation\r\n  error, instead of discarding it. `StatementBuilder.build()` already did this;\r\n  `Statement(contents=...)` did not, so a rejected digest algorithm, a missing\r\n  field and a bad `_type` were indistinguishable.\r\n  ([#1846](https://github.com/sigstore/sigstore-python/pull/1846))\r\n* `Verifier` now raises `VerificationError` when the trusted root contains no\r\n  transparency log instances, instead of leaking a raw `IndexError`\r\n  ([#1880](https://github.com/sigstore/sigstore-python/pull/1880))"}